{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"064b753fb5172d4815b413b05a26aea3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about iTerm2 DynamicProfiles - specifically:\n1. Standard storage path\n2. JSON top-level schema (required fields: Name, Guid, color keys)\n3. Whether a Profile with the same name would override user's existing Profile\n\nThey want mechanically verifiable command snippets (ls, defaults read, jq) and want the answer in Chinese.\n\nThis is a straightforward knowledge question about iTerm2 DynamicProfiles. Let me answer based on known facts.\n\niTerm2 Dynamic Profiles are stored in:\n- `~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/DynamicProfiles/`\n\nThe JSON schema for a dynamic profile:\n- Top-level must have: `Name`, `Guid`\n- Color keys are under a `Colors` object\n\nWhether same name overrides: iTerm2 uses `Name` as the identifier. If a dynamic profile has the same `Name` as an existing user profile, it will override/merge. But actually, looking at iTerm2 docs, dynamic profiles with the same name as an existing profile will override the built-in one - it's based on Name matching.\n\nLet me provide the answer with command snippets.","signature":"2e39baee610263b8ef9ba71df7b24ddb4f54d634737033049a103f256e452f66"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":159,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26942,"cache_read_input_tokens":20205},"service_tier":"standard","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6531f86-78a4-4bf1-89e0-26a2c23a4c48","uuid":"c4e668c8-7e09-43a1-9c35-1f40a9acb750"}
